cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below. A WSRI computational-essay publication is in preparation; update preferred-citation when it acquires an identifier."
type: software
title: "black-box: Evaluating black-box physics through optical emulation — machine-verified quantum contextuality"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kolcz"
    given-names: "Hubert"
    email: "kolcz.h@gmail.com"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hubertkolcz/black-box"
abstract: >-
  Machine-verified computational essays certifying black-box quantumness against
  classical optical emulation: KCBS-pentagon graph invariants and Global-Exclusivity
  correlation certificates, contextual fraction and signed negativity, pentagon-mesh
  composition theorems with epsilon-certificates, a pre-registered black-box
  certification protocol, Abramsky-Brandenburger sheaf/Cech-cohomology certificates,
  a signaling-taxonomy extension, and a structural result on the classical
  emulatability of analogue-Hawking-radiation witnesses. Includes the Wolfram paclet
  HubertKolcz/BlackBox.
keywords:
  - quantum contextuality
  - KCBS
  - Lovasz theta
  - exclusivity principle
  - contextual fraction
  - sheaf cohomology
  - MBQC
  - dynamical Lie algebra
  - black-box certification
  - analogue Hawking radiation
